  "id": "COMPOUND:32766 - PROTEIN:4951",
  "verbalization": "The visible evidence suggests a potential relationship between (2R)-2-[4-(7-Chloroquinoxalin-2-Yl)Oxyphenoxy]Propanoic Acid and HL-60, a human leukemia cell line. This compound is identified as a target of multiple molecules, including Lysine-specific demethylase 2A, which is a key enzyme involved in epigenetic regulation. Lysine-specific demethylase 2A is further targeted by additional compounds, such as (2S,9R,13R,14S,15R,17R)-14-acetyloxy-16-hydroxy-4-methoxy-2,6,14,17-tetramethyl-3,11-dioxo-10-oxatetracyclo[7.7.1.02,7.013,17]heptadec-4-en-15-yl acetate and (2E)-3-(4-methylphenyl)-N-(2-phenylethyl)prop-2-enamide, all of which are targeted by HL-60. This indicates that the compound may exert its effects through interactions with epigenetic regulators, potentially influencing cellular processes in HL-60 cells. The evidence suggests a possible mechanism involving the modulation of epigenetic pathways, though the exact molecular interactions remain to be fully elucidated.",
